
# Commit message example
# ----------------------
# [COMPONENT] A short but descriptive summary
#
# Problem: what goes wrong, as it was observed.
#
# Why: the rule, contract or invariant that makes it wrong.
#
# How: what the change does.
# ----------------------
# * [COMPONENT] should usually be the name of the CMake module, written
#   in all caps. Use several tags, such as [NTOS:KE][HAL], only when
#   one change needs them.
# * Summary should be imperative (not past tense) and not end with a
#   period.
# * For a short feature commit, start the body with "feat:" instead of
#   Problem/Why/How. Never put "feat:" in the summary.
# * A wording, typo or formatting change may keep the summary only.
# * For ABI and layout changes, name the evidence.
# * There must be a newline between summary and description.
# * The width of the description is arbitrary, but it is a good idea
#   to wrap the text by 72 chars.
